{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>Hear</b> — If the poet is speaking about David, [it is addressed] to the queen-consort, and the sense is: forget your people — like the usage of 'your people, my people' — that you should convert and return to the Torah of David. And if he speaks about the Messiah, the meaning of <b>daughter</b> is congregation, as in 'daughter of Judah,' after the manner of 'to serve HaShem with one accord.'"], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 45, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:30:54.697762564Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}